\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Overview of CS4M. The pipeline first converts host logs into data-flow provenance events and runtime-visible node/action semantics, then learns compact node and action embeddings. During online inference, CS4M reads pre-update source and destination states, constructs an E4 dual semantic prediction context, scores the residual before updating state, and emits event and node alert evidence. OFSM compresses active state storage after alerting; ground truth is used only later for evaluation.}}{8}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cs4m-overview}{{2}{8}{Overview of CS4M. The pipeline first converts host logs into data-flow provenance events and runtime-visible node/action semantics, then learns compact node and action embeddings. During online inference, CS4M reads pre-update source and destination states, constructs an E4 dual semantic prediction context, scores the residual before updating state, and emits event and node alert evidence. OFSM compresses active state storage after alerting; ground truth is used only later for evaluation}{figure.2}{}}
